<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chilperic I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 539–584</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Chilperic I of Neustria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chilperic I was a Merovingian king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> who ruled the western kingdom of Neustria from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soissons">Soissons</a> from 561 until his murder in 584. A son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlothar-i">Chlothar I</a>, he fought long wars against his brothers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigebert-i">Sigebert I</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guntram">Guntram</a>, and his feud with Austrasia, waged with his wife <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fredegund">Fredegund</a> against Queen Brunhild, dominated Frankish politics. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregory-of-tours">Gregory of Tours</a> portrayed him as cruel and greedy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chilperic-i.jpg" alt="Chilperic I" width="320" height="149" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: elsen.eu · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tremissis_-_Chilperic_I_-_Vermand_-_Transparent_Ver.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
